    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (82.24) and **Junior Caminero** (78.33), our strongest plays of the day. Despite facing a veteran arm like Scherzer, **Junior Caminero** projects well due to an ideal batting order slot and favorable park conditions, while **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in start, benefiting from elite xwOBA metrics and a significant platoon edge against Walbert Ure\u00f1a. **Trea Turner** (72.36) and **Kyle Schwarber** (69.60) also profile as high-leverage assets today; they both capitalize on a favorable matchup against Alcantara, with **Trea Turner** specifically bolstered by a positive BvP history and the prime #2 spot in the order, which maximizes our stolen base potential in this scarcest of categories.\n\nEfficiency in the middle infield remains critical, leading to the deployment of **Caleb Durbin** (66.32) over the bench. **Caleb Durbin** is a priority start because of the specific tactical edge provided by Pfaadt\u2019s slow delivery, which boosts his stolen base expectancy significantly. The most difficult bench decision involved **Colt Keith** (46.18), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Colt Keith** possesses high utility, he faced a brutal matchup against Skenes\u2014an elite arm with a low xERA and an efficient catcher pop time\u2014which suppressed his scoring ceiling compared to our starting infielders. We continue to monitor **Kazuma Okamoto** (37.96) and **Christian Yelich** (53.59), both of whom are reliant on \"Lineup Pending\" status; should they drop lower in the order than projected, their marginal scores will force us to re-evaluate their presence in today's cap-sensitive structure.",
